# =============================================================================
# experiment/tgrad/tgrad_T-20_h1.00_10s_G0.opts — 10 SECONDS at -20 C, saturated,
# NO temperature gradient.
#
# CONFIGURATION CHECK, NOT SCIENCE. Identical physics to tgrad_T-20_h1.00_90d_G0
# (same temperature, humidity, zero gradient, BCs and kinetics) with t_final
# cut to 10 s, so a new geometry can be opened in ParaView and eyeballed before
# it costs an HPC allocation. 10 s is ~0.02 tau_sub — nothing measurable moves.
# Zero-gradient twin of Tgrad_T-20_G50_10s.opts.
#
# WHAT TO LOOK AT. The initial condition is written as sol_00000.dat BEFORE
# any solve (OutputMonitor, src/monitoring.c:298), together with igasol.dat —
# so the configuration is on disk within seconds of launch even if the run is
# interrupted. Everything after that is confirmation the solver is happy with
# the mesh.
#
# CHECKLIST for the wedge band (2D_wedge_band):
#   - the band spans wall to wall, touching both
#   - BOTH menisci meet the walls at 90 deg — the single most important
#     visual, since the whole migration prediction rests on the contact angle.
#     The band edges should read as ARCS bowing toward the narrow end, not as
#     straight cuts; a straight cut means the apex/radii are wrong.
#   - the diffuse band is uniform in width along both arcs
#   - temperature is FLAT (no gradient) — if it ramps, the wrong experiment
#     file is in play and the result would be about the gradient, not the pore
#
# -outp 1 overrides the time-synchronised output of the longer G0 files: with
# only a handful of steps we want every one of them.
# =============================================================================

-t_final 1.0e1                          # 10 seconds

-temp -20.0
-humidity 1.00
-grad_temp0 0.0,0.0,0.0                  # control: no gradient

-flag_BC_Tfix 1                          # pin wall temperatures (uniform, no gradient)

-outp 1                                  # every step (few enough to want them all)

-beta_sub0 5.9216e5                      # K&P beta0 at -20 C, alpha_c = 1.341e-2
-d0_sub0 1.0166e-9                        # physical capillary length at -20 C

-dtmax 2.0                               # cap dt so 10 s is a few steps, not one
-dtCFL 1
-dtCFL_dphimax 0.2
